            <ArticleTitle>A simple clinical model predicted diabetes progression among prediabetic individuals.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e34-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.diabres.2012.04.018</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We followed 1372 prediabetic individuals aged ≥ 20 years and documented 278 incident diabetes cases. Family history of diabetes, blood pressure, waist, high-density lipoprotein cholesterol, and FPG independently associated with diabetes progression among women. Among men, family history of premature CVD, waist, and FPG remained independently associated with diabetes progression.</AbstractText>
